{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-58579","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68557","text":"TickTickClock Documentation"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58581","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68558","marks":["bold"],"text":"Every tick is a learning opportunity. Every pattern has a rhythm. Temporal intelligence that never forgets."}]}],"id":"blk-58580","kind":"quote"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58583","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68559","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-68560","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-68561","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-68562","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-68563","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-68564","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-68565","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-58582","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-58584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68566","text":"Welcome to the documentation hub for "},{"id":"spn-68567","marks":["bold"],"text":"TickTickClock"},{"id":"spn-68568","text":" — the temporal intelligence layer for the [&] Protocol ecosystem. TickTickClock provides time-series anomaly detection, forecasting, and pattern recognition as continual learning services."}]},{"id":"blk-58585","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68569","text":"TickTickClock is the "},{"id":"spn-68570","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-68571","text":" primitive provider, exposing "},{"id":"spn-68572","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-68573","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68574","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.forecast"},{"id":"spn-68575","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-68576","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.pattern"},{"id":"spn-68577","text":" capability contracts. It does not store business data, host agents, or manage workflows — it ingests temporal signals, learns their structure continuously, and returns intelligence to upstream consumers."}]},{"id":"blk-58586","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68578","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58587","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68579","text":"The Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-58588","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68580","text":"Time-series intelligence in production systems is fragmented. Anomaly detection runs as a batch job. Forecasting lives in a notebook. Pattern detection is a dashboard someone checks on Mondays. None of these systems learn continuously, and none of them talk to each other."}]},{"id":"blk-58589","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68581","text":"Meanwhile, underlying models suffer from catastrophic forgetting — retrained monthly on a window of recent data, discarding everything about long-range seasonality. Multi-timescale temporal behavior requires multi-timescale memory, and no production system provides it."}]},{"id":"blk-58590","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68582","text":"TickTickClock solves this with:"}]},{"id":"blk-58591","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58593","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68583","marks":["bold"],"text":"Continual learning"},{"id":"spn-68584","text":" — models update at inference time, no batch retraining"}]}],"id":"blk-58592","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68585","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multi-timescale memory"},{"id":"spn-68586","text":" — fast (seconds), medium (hours), slow (days), glacial (months)"}]}],"id":"blk-58594","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58597","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68587","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming-first"},{"id":"spn-68588","text":" — designed for unbounded streams, not fixed datasets"}]}],"id":"blk-58596","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58599","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68589","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge-capable"},{"id":"spn-68590","text":" — SQLite + Bumblebee on constrained devices"}]}],"id":"blk-58598","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68591","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58601","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68592","text":"Documentation Map"}]},{"id":"blk-58602","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Homepages\n\n[&] Ampersand Box <https://ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous <https://graphonomous.com>\nBendScript <https://bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems <https://webhost.systems>\nAgentelic <https://agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic <https://agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic <https://delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic <https://deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt <https://fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic <https://geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience <https://opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt <https://specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock <https://ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-58603","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 1\n:caption: Root Docs\n\n[&] Protocol Docs <https://docs.ampersandboxdesign.com>\nGraphonomous Docs <https://docs.graphonomous.com>\nBendScript Docs <https://docs.bendscript.com>\nWebHost.Systems Docs <https://docs.webhost.systems>\nAgentelic Docs <https://docs.agentelic.com>\nAgenTroMatic Docs <https://docs.agentromatic.com>\nDelegatic Docs <https://docs.delegatic.com>\nDeliberatic Docs <https://docs.deliberatic.com>\nFleetPrompt Docs <https://docs.fleetprompt.com>\nGeoFleetic Docs <https://docs.geofleetic.com>\nOpenSentience Docs <https://docs.opensentience.org>\nSpecPrompt Docs <https://docs.specprompt.com>\nTickTickClock Docs <https://docs.ticktickclock.com>"},{"id":"blk-58604","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":maxdepth: 2\n:caption: TickTickClock Docs\n\nspec/README"},{"id":"blk-58605","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68593","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58606","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68594","text":"[&] Capability Contracts"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-58608","sp